# Sidisi, Regent of the Mire: "{T}, Sacrifice a creature you control with mana value X other than Sidisi: Return target creature card with
# mana value X plus 1 from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only as a sorcery." X is announced first (CR 107.3a, 601.2b) and is
# the mana value of the creature sacrificed; the target is chosen after it (CR 601.2c) and must have mana value X + 1 (CR 202.3).
# Turn 1 Bot1 casts Sidisi (mana value 2) and Bog Rats (1). Turn 2 Bot2 casts its own Child of Night (2) and Bolts it. On turn 3 Bot1 casts
# Child of Night, which Bot2 Bolts: each player has a Child of Night (mana value 2) in its graveyard. With a Mishra's Bauble on the stack the
# ability is refused (sorcery speed, CR 307.1). X = 2 is refused (the only creature with mana value 2 is Sidisi herself: "other than
# Sidisi"). X = 1: the Child in Bot2's graveyard is refused ("your graveyard"), Bot1's own is chosen, and Bog Rats is sacrificed.
# Sidisi taps (it is her own {T}), and the Child comes back untapped.

